      "text": "Note that the Gates of the cascodes M3 and M4 are now at ground, which is the lowest voltage available. The maximum output voltage V is 0.7 V as outmax we need at least 0.15 V V DS per transistor. It is clear that for deep submicron CMOS, where the V decreases to as little T as 0.3 V, the supply voltage can be as low as 0.6 V. Quite a low value indeed!!"
